    q1=prim[prim.candidate=='Q1'].iloc[0];q2=prim[prim.candidate=='Q2'].iloc[0];dp=depth[(depth.scope=='Home_all_common_support')&(depth.definition=='Q1_AA')&(depth.threshold==2)].iloc[0];de=depth[(depth.scope==_private_literal('private_d54419bd68c77be2'))&(depth.definition=='Q1_AA')&(depth.threshold==2)].iloc[0]
    lines=['# Q1/Q2 candidate associations, detection depth and evidence interpretation (v7)','',
      '## Main interpretation','',
      f'Q1 remains a prioritized circulating candidate: at the fixed AA≥2 definition it was observed in28/56 N+ versus18/70 N0 patients (50.0% versus25.7%; Fisher P={q1.fisher_P:.5f}, BH2 q={q1.crude_BH_q:.5f}). This is an exploratory patient-level enrichment within the frozen retrospective comparison; correction across the two re-evaluated candidates does not remove the selection effects of their historical nomination. After adjustment for age, sex, acquisition batch, assigned-read depth, unique-AA load and recorded neoadjuvant treatment, the Firth OR was{q1.adjusted_OR:.3f} (95%profile-likelihood CI{q1.adjusted_OR_low:.3f}–{q1.adjusted_OR_high:.3f}; P={q1.adjusted_P:.4f}, BH2 q={q1.adjusted_BH_q:.4f}). This supports a candidate signal whose independence from the measured covariates remains uncertain. It is not a validated N classifier.', '',
      f'Q2 showed46/56 versus46/70 carriers (82.1% versus65.7%; Fisher P={q2.fisher_P:.5f}, BH2 q={q2.crude_BH_q:.5f}); adjusted OR{q2.adjusted_OR:.3f} (95%CI{q2.adjusted_OR_low:.3f}–{q2.adjusted_OR_high:.3f}; q={q2.adjusted_BH_q:.4f}). Q2 is another nominated candidate, not an experimental negative control.', '',
      'Sensitivity q values use the complete118 nonprimary comparisons, assigning P=1 internally to non-estimable entries and restoring their reported q to NA. The original lane protocol specified available tests; this conservative denominator expansion was made during the final reporting audit and is recorded in MULTIPLICITY_CORRECTION_20261004.md. Primary BH2 results, raw P values and effect estimates are unchanged.', '',
      '## Depth directly quantified','',
      'Median assigned QC depth was6,931,799 inHome and1,830,622 inExternal. Of137 Home patients,135 had enough assigned reads for thinning to every observed External depth; the remaining2 were excluded only from the common-support transport calculation. Each of the202 External depths was evaluated against every eligible Home patient using exact finite-population hypergeometric tails. This is a transport counterfactual, not a reconstruction of unobserved External clones.', '',
      f"At AA≥2, thinning reduced expected Q1 carriage from53/135(39.26%) at the original Home depths to{dp.expected_External_prevalence * 100:.2f}% at the External depths: {dp.expected_External_carriers:.2f}/202 expected detections (95%Home-patient bootstrap CI{dp.expected_External_carriers_low:.2f}–{dp.expected_External_carriers_high:.2f}), compared with the observed0/202. Under this empirical abundance/capture transport model, the probability of zero detections was{dp.probability_zero_External_carriers:.3g}{_private_literal('private_b276c97a1c27c2e9')}{de.expected_External_carriers:.2f} (CI{de.expected_External_carriers_low:.2f}–{de.expected_External_carriers_high:.2f}), with zero probability{de.probability_zero_External_carriers:.3g}. Thus sequencing depth substantially affects detectability, but reducing depth alone does not reproduce the observed External absence.", '',
      _private_literal('private_64e7d1af46736e41'), '',
      '## Same-fold prediction results','',
      'All60 outer/inner partitions matched the original saved patient partitions exactly. Recomputed M1 probabilities differed by at most8.33×10⁻¹⁷. Preprocessing and C selection remained inside training folds, and duplicate bootstrap draws stayed grouped by the original patient identifier. Both candidate additions completed200 full-pipeline resamples. The historical nomination process is outside this CV boundary, so results are conditional on those nominations.']
    for q in ['Q1','Q2']:
        m=metrics[metrics.model=='M1_'+q].iloc[0];x=inc[inc.candidate==q].iloc[0];c=ci[(ci.candidate==q)&(ci.metric=='delta_log_loss')].iloc[0];auc=ci[(ci.candidate==q)&(ci.metric=='delta_AUROC')].iloc[0]
        lines+=['',f'M1+{q}: AUROC{m.AUROC:.3f}; paired Δlog-loss={x.delta_log_loss:.5f} (95%full-pipeline CI{c.ci_low:.5f}–{c.ci_high:.5f}; positive means improvement), ΔAUROC={x.delta_AUROC:.4f} (CI{auc.ci_low:.4f}–{auc.ci_high:.4f}). All comparison, calibration, external and leave-batch-out results are retained in models/.']
    lines += ['', 'The baseline M1 AUROC was0.610. Candidate-only learned OOF scores and the binary marker’s observed carriage contrast answer different questions: pooled OOF values also vary with training-fold fitted intercepts and regularization. Do not substitute the apparent binary-carriage ROC for held-out model validation. Normalized clonality defined as1−normalizedShannon is algebraically redundant with the existing summary endpoint; the old complete repertoire tests remain unchanged.', '', '## External recurrence and the reported experiment','',
      'Independent public source records support recurrence of the complete Q1 amino-acid sequence in an archivedCRC tumor and7serialPBMC repertoires from one Le2017 participant. The dominant receptor branch isV5-4/J1-4, with a different nucleotide sequence from the Home designatedV5-5 target; the designated Home NT was not observed in these8records. This is useful sequence recurrence evidence, not a new functional binding assay, a multi-participant diagnostic validation, or proof that the designated Home NT assay was validated externally.', '',
      'The historical manuscript reports a separate sequence-specific TaqMan experiment in12CRC and6healthy samples, with allCRC described as quantifiable and allhealthy belowLOQ. Complete well-level records and sample mapping remain unrecovered. Accordingly the report supplies assay-feasibility evidence at a reported-data tier; no fabricated Ct scatter or rederived diagnostic estimate is supplied. The reported N comparison wasP=.699. This should not be presented as positive experimental validation of N discrimination.', '',
      'Source-stratified Q1 prevalence remains53/137 HomeCRC,0/202 ExternalCRC and0/87 healthy reference libraries at the matched numerical≥2threshold. Patient versus library units and RNA-read versus source-template counts are preserved; the between-source contrast is not treated as a confounding-free estimate of CRC specificity.', '',
      '## Reproduction and audit','',
      'Run from the remote revision_v7 directory:', '', '```sh', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n.py prepare', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n.py associations', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n.py depth', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n_models.py --jobs 8 --bootstrap 200', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n_verify.py --models', 'PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 code/v7_q1_depth_n_finalize.py', '```', '',
      'Source hashes are in input_manifest.tsv. All counts, covariates, exclusions, definition/threshold sensitivities, OOF predictions, grouped fold memberships, complete bootstrap outputs and negative controls are retained. Scripts and data are bound in output_manifest.tsv and delivery_receipt.json. Frozen v6 source files were read only.']
    (OUT/'Q1_DEPTH_N_REPORT.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
    files=sorted([p for p in OUT.rglob('*') if p.is_file() and p.name not in ['output_manifest.tsv','delivery_receipt.json'] and not p.name.endswith('.log')])
    files+=sorted((ROOT/'code').glob('v7_q1_depth_n*.py'))
    manifest=pd.DataFrame([{'path':str(p),'relative_path':str(p.relative_to(ROOT)),'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':sha(p)} for p in files]);write(manifest,OUT/'output_manifest.tsv')
    receipt={'status':'PASS','scope':'Q1_Q2_association_depth_models_source_evidence','seed':20261004,'n_Home':137,'n_Home_knownN':126,'n_External':202,'n_External_knownN':163,'primary_adjusted_tests':2,'sensitivity_grid_rows':len(sens),'sensitivity_BH_family_n':118,'multiplicity_correction':'MULTIPLICITY_CORRECTION_20261004.md','fullpipeline_bootstraps_per_candidate':200,'verification_checks':verified['checks'],'input_manifest_sha256':sha(OUT/'input_manifest.tsv'),'protocol_sha256':sha(OUT/'PROTOCOL.md'),'output_manifest_sha256':sha(OUT/'output_manifest.tsv'),'output_files':len(files),'source_v6_read_only':True,'analysis_computation_host':'codex-remote','plots_owned_by':'figures_v7_lane','files':{'report':'Q1_DEPTH_N_REPORT.md','primary':'N_association_primary.tsv','depth':'depth/counterfactual_summary.tsv','model_increment':'models/paired_model_increment.tsv','model_CI':'models/full_pipeline_paired_ci.tsv','source_audit':'external_experiment_evidence_audit.tsv'}}
